course: dictionary
lesson: 3803
title: Forecaster: someone who predicts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A forecaster is a person who says what will probably happen. A weather forecaster tells us about rain, sun and storms before they arrive, using maps and science.
explain: Context helps you here. «Weather satellites photograph clouds and measure temperatures, which helps forecasters predict storms days ahead.» Predict means to say what will happen before it happens, so a forecaster is someone who predicts.
explain: Sometimes a forecaster changes their mind. «Good readers change their predictions as they go, like a weather forecaster who looks out of the window again.» A forecaster looks at new evidence and updates their guess, just as a good reader does.
fact: A forecaster is a person who says what will probably happen.
fact: «Forecaster» can mean a weather forecaster, who predicts the weather, or someone who predicts money or business changes.
fact: Forecasts are predictions, not certainties, so they can sometimes be wrong.
fact: «Predict» means to say what will happen before it happens.
fact: Forecasters use data from satellites and weather stations to make their predictions.
exercise: «Weather forecasters watch the air pressure: high pressure usually means calm, settled days.» What does high pressure usually bring? | Clouds and wind | Snow only | *Calm, settled days | Storms and heavy rain
exercise: What does a forecaster do? | *Says what will probably happen | Plays music on the radio | Only takes photographs of clouds | Makes the weather happen
exercise: Which person is a forecaster in the second meaning? | A teacher who marks spelling tests | A cook who bakes bread | *Someone who predicts changes in money and business | A bus driver
test: Why might a forecast turn out to be wrong? | Because forecasts are written in pencil | Because the sun never shines on a forecast day | Because forecasters always tell lies on purpose | *Because forecasts are predictions, and the future is not certain
test: «Weather satellites photograph clouds and measure temperatures, which helps forecasters predict storms days ahead.» What helps forecasters predict storms days ahead? | A pair of trainers | *Weather satellites | A bicycle | A kettle
exam: «Good readers change their predictions as they go, like a weather forecaster who looks out of the window again.» What does a forecaster do when they see new evidence? | They stop making predictions | They only forecast on Sundays | They always forecast sunshine | *They change their prediction as they learn more
